The '''cloak spell''' is a mixed [[Spells|spell]] that allows the user to preform magic remotley through the cloak, and control the cloak's movment from afar.

==Description==
The cloak spell contains a central body and a windowway ring that loops around the spell. The spell's main body contains a central vision sigil with eye signs placed on 4 of the eight ends of the vision sigil, with wind sigils on the other 4. Along the ring of the glyph, 4 bend and 4 puppett keystones are placed.{{Ref|m|27|22}} This spell was used by Sasaran on his cloak, and it functioned to allow him to control the cloak remotley while preforming spells through it, hiding his main body elsewhere.{{Ref|m|17|33}} The cloak spell is a fusion of the [[Gathering Shadows|gathering shadows]] spell, which drapes the object in shaodw, the [[Flying Puppet of Diversion|flying puppet of diversion]] spell, which makes the object fly through the air, and the [[Windowway Spell|windowway spell]], which allows objects to pass through it from one location to another.

==Usage==
The spell is used by [[Sasaran]], who has it written on the inside of his cloak. He was seen using the cloak while in the [[Serpentback Cave]] while [[Qifrey|Qifrey's]] [[Qifrey's Atelier|students]] were taking [[The Sincerity of the Shield]] test, and was employed heavily during his fight with Qifrey.{{Ref|m|27|22}}

